---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.tsx'
import '../index.css'
---

<Layout title="About - PhyloGuessr">
  <div class="game">
    <Header client:load />
    <div class="about-page">
      <h2>About PhyloGuessr</h2>

      <h3>Data sources</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Taxonomy from <a
            href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/taxonomy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">NCBI Taxonomy</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          Images from <a
            href="https://en.wikipedia.org/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Contribute</h3>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/cmdcolin/phyloguessr"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
        > · <a
          href="https://github.com/cmdcolin/phyloguessr/issues"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Report bugs or suggest new comparisons</a
        > · <a href="/donate">Donate</a>
      </p>

      <h3>FAQ</h3>
      <h4>What is the relationship between taxonomy and phylogeny?</h4>
      <p>
        Taxonomy is for naming and grouping organisms, while phylogeny describes
        evolutionary history. While taxonomy aims to mirror phylogeny, they can
        differ in some cases due to evolving understanding or legacy categorizations. We
        use NCBI Taxonomy, which is a classification system and may not reflect
        every recent phylogenetic discovery.
      </p>

      <h4>Where did the idea come from?</h4>
      <p>
        I once attended a 'Science on Tap' trivia night, and they played a game
        like this on powerpoint slides. It was quite fun. I had a small list of
        funny evolutionary relationships on my 'oddbiology' github repo also and
        thought it would be fun to make it into a game. If you have any ideas
        for the game feel free to contact me! And yes, the name is inspired by
        the GeoGuessr game.
      </p>

      <h4>Can I use this for my own trivia night or classroom?</h4>
      <p>
        Yes! Feel free to use it for any purpose. You can even change it for
        your needs. It is free and open source
      </p>

      <h3>Use of AI</h3>
      <p>
        I used Claude Code extensively to help development, and even to create
        scenario ideas, and narrate the 'fun facts'. I know it's a weird thing
        but I feel it helps to be transparent about such things. If you find any
        issues, please report on
        <a
          href="https://github.com/cmdcolin/phyloguessr/issues"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
        > or email <a href="mailto:colin.diesh@gmail.com"
          >colin.diesh@gmail.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
